all right we now have a special  prosecutor in the Trump Russia  investigation after Donald Trump fired  FBI director James Comey last week we  had the revelation earlier this week  that Donald Trump allegedly asked James  Comey to drop the FBI's investigation  into disgraced former national security  adviser Michael Flynn  we heard calls from both sides mostly  from Democrats but from some Republicans  as well for an independent counsel also  known as a special prosecutor to be  assigned to oversee this entire Trump  Russia investigation and one of the  reasons for this is that and and this is  a fear that escalated with the would be  the firing of James Comey was the fear  that Donald Trump would appoint a new  FBI director that would just favor the  President and compromise the integrity  of yet another investigation not that we  haven't seen other investigations into  Trump Russia already compromised a very  reasonable concern some Republicans have  still been resisting the idea of  bringing in an outsider but the Justice  Department has a secound to the pressure  you could say and it was announced that  Deputy Attorney General rod Rosenstein  he's the guy who's been acting as  Attorney General in all Russia related  matters after Jeff Sessions recused  himself with the exception of Jeff  Sessions recommending the firing of  James Comey in any case rod Rosenstein  has appointed former FBI director robert  muller as special prosecutor to  facilitate this investigation into the  Trump Russia scandal if that name sounds  familiar it's because again he was the  FBI director appointed by George W Bush  in oh one served until 2013 when James  Comey took over so the obvious question  is are we going to get an unbiased and  fair investigation as a result of this  on the one hand yeah Muller's a  Republican he still technically answers  to Rosenstein and Trump but he's not  known as a partisan hack he has no  direct ties to Donald Trump that we know  of as of right now no major  controversies in his past he stood up  when george w bush was abusing his power  Obama liked him enough to extend his  term when he was FBI director and I  think most people know that  you'll be more impartial than whoever  Trump would have appointed to replace  James Comey yeah and that is good news  it just comes as a surprise though  because Rosenstein was as you mentioned  very influential in the firing of James  Comey yeah so it seemed as this he was  trying to sweep this whole Russia  investigation under the rug so this is a  complete 180 very good news especially  because the FBI investigation and the  house investigation have both been  significantly undermined in the  documents discredited to some degree a  quote from Deputy Attorney General rod  Rosenstein what I have determined is  that based upon the unique circumstances  the Public Interest requires me to place  this investigation under the authority  of a person who exercises a degree of  independence from the normal chain of  command a special counsel was necessary  in order for the American people to have  full confidence in the outcome according  to White House officials Donald Trump  didn't find out about the appointment of  a special prosecutor until after the  appointment was made and he reportedly  wasn't happy about it at all which is  terrific and Trump responded to all of  this in a statement yesterday saying  quote as I have stated many times a  thorough investigation will confirm what  we already know there was no collusion  between my campaign and any foreign  entity I look forward to this matter  concluding quickly yeah I bet Trump  wants this to conclude quickly that  that's obviously clear the Department of  Justice sort of had no choice so I know  you're reading in due to rod Rosenstein  decision as a sort of 180 did they  really have a choice I mean as you as  you pointed out the FBI investigation  had been tarnished by the firing of  James Comey the house investigation has  been a joke for months at this point the  entire executive branch would look so  corrupt if they didn't do this and they  probably know that but yet it is still  curious that one of the guys who  recommended firing Comey now says let's  put in a special prosecutor and they're  also looking out for themselves too  right they have to keep their own hands  clean and yeah it is it is remarkable  that Trump is trying to speed up this  investigation because as it goes on  there's more of a chance of them finding  something that's why he asked Comey to  end the investigation into Michael Flynn  saying he's a good guy though yeah Greg  no good no good guy has ever committed a  crime worthy of investigation Democratic  Senator Ben Cardin of Maryland said  yesterday quote rather than make this go  away Deputy Attorney General Rosenstein  has taken an important step toward  restoring the credibility of the DOJ and  FBI in this most serious matter  so like James Comey Robert Muller will  not have to consult with or inform the  Justice Department nor the White House  about the investigation the FBI has  already said we are not going to be  keeping the White House up-to-date on  what is going on with this investigation  Trump will undoubtedly replace Comey  eventually with someone who is friendly  to trump and we definitely don't want  that person leading the investigation so  now at least we have the appearance that  the DOJ investigation is getting more  serious we'll see if it actually does it  would have been better if an independent  prosecutor could have been appointed by  Congress because then Trump wouldn't  even be able to fire that person but  Trump would not be able to fire Robert  Mulder without significant scrutiny I  mean I think that these things take time  Watergate took about a year and a half  before Richard Nixon eventually resigned  so I think there's an urgency to try to  get Trump out of office now but it could  take years  it could and it also might not be that  great for Democrats and I'm going to out  next week we're going to dig into that  but people online already talking about  oh this is the beginning of the end I  think it's a little soon to say that for  now

